# tool -> the skills that stop working without it
#
# Format:  <command>|<plain-english consequence>|<comma-separated skill names>
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, rather than the strings living inside setup.sh:
# a hardcoded consequence string drifts silently. When a skill is added, removed, or
# stops shelling out to a tool, nothing makes the installer's failure message wrong in
# a way anyone notices — it just quietly lies. Here the mapping is data, so it can be
# regenerated from the shipped skill set and diffed. AC-YTI-016 requires the message to
# be drawn from a committed map for exactly that reason; an earlier version of this
# change hardcoded them and was caught in pre-merge review 2026-08-10.
#
# Derived 2026-08-10 by scanning what the 51 shipped skills actually invoke (not what
# they mention in prose — an early scan counted 65 skills "needing ImageMagick" because
# the English word "convert" matched; the real count is zero).
#
# Regenerate after changing the shipped skill set:
#   grep -rlE 'subprocess.*ffmpeg|ffmpeg -|`ffmpeg' .claude/skills --include=*.md --include=*.py --include=*.sh

ffmpeg|video skills can't run|00-longform-to-shortform,00-social-content
ffprobe|video skills can't read clip lengths|00-longform-to-shortform,00-social-content
yt-dlp|YouTube skills can't fetch anything|00-longform-to-shortform,00-social-content,meta-skill-system-creator,tool-youtube
jq|the long-to-short pipeline can't parse its data|00-longform-to-shortform
gh|session wrap-up can't reach GitHub|meta-wrap-up
node|memory can't run at all|<the memory engine>
python3|most skill scripts can't run, and the harness gates can't fire|<most skills>
playwright|browser-driving skills fail|00-social-content,mkt-brand-voice,mkt-visual-identity,viz-excalidraw-diagram,viz-image-gen,eng-harness
